WEBVTT

00:00:17.356 --> 00:00:19.567
I think he wants us to
pick up what he left off.

00:00:20.399 --> 00:00:22.365
Saving people, hunting things...

00:00:22.366 --> 00:00:23.493
Family business.

00:00:24.572 --> 00:00:27.543
I don't understand the blind
faith you have in the man.

00:00:27.544 --> 00:00:29.054
It's called being a good son!

00:00:31.512 --> 00:00:34.601
You were just pissed off you
couldn't control me anymore!

00:00:42.596 --> 00:00:44.070
If only your boys

00:00:44.718 --> 00:00:46.602
Knew how much their daddy loved them.

00:00:55.110 --> 00:00:55.968
Dad?

00:01:01.826 --> 00:01:04.063
Did he say anything to you? No.

00:01:06.597 --> 00:01:08.421
I'm dealing with dad's death.

00:01:09.606 --> 00:01:10.573
Are you?

00:03:03.188 --> 00:03:04.562
Listen to her purr.

00:03:04.566 --> 00:03:06.233
You ever heard anything so sweet?

00:03:06.235 --> 00:03:09.042
If you two want to get a
room, just let me know, Dean.

00:03:09.047 --> 00:03:10.763
Oh, don't listen to him, baby.

00:03:10.768 --> 00:03:12.031
He doesn't understand.

00:03:13.335 --> 00:03:14.763
You're in a good mood.

00:03:14.768 --> 00:03:15.952
Why shouldn't I be?

00:03:16.828 --> 00:03:17.790
No reason.

00:03:17.805 --> 00:03:19.013
I got my car,

00:03:19.138 --> 00:03:20.272
I got a case.

00:03:20.536 --> 00:03:21.571
Things are looking up.

00:03:23.387 --> 00:03:26.733
You hear of a couple of severed
heads and a pile of dead cows,

00:03:26.738 --> 00:03:28.442
And you're mr. Sunshine.

00:03:29.236 --> 00:03:30.671
How far to Red Lodge?

00:03:31.288 --> 00:03:33.423
Uh, about another 300 miles.

00:03:34.205 --> 00:03:35.093
Good.

00:03:40.037 --> 00:03:42.390
The murder investigation is ongoing,

00:03:42.407 --> 00:03:44.602
And that's all I can share
with the press at this time.

00:03:44.607 --> 00:03:46.491
Sure, sure, we understand
that. But just for the record,

00:03:46.616 --> 00:03:48.311
You found the first uh...

00:03:48.695 --> 00:03:50.043
Head last week, correct?

00:03:50.687 --> 00:03:52.573
Okay, and the other, a...

00:03:52.576 --> 00:03:55.032
Christina Flannigan?
That was two days ago.

00:03:55.035 --> 00:03:56.303
Excuse me, Sir.

00:03:57.376 --> 00:03:58.412
Thank you.

00:03:58.886 --> 00:04:00.572
Sorry, boys, time's up.

00:04:00.577 --> 00:04:01.830
We're done here. One last question.

00:04:01.837 --> 00:04:03.330
What about the cattle? Excuse me?

00:04:03.335 --> 00:04:04.703
You know, the cows found dead,

00:04:04.835 --> 00:04:08.103
Split open, drained...
Over a dozen cases.

00:04:09.118 --> 00:04:09.982
What about them?

00:04:09.987 --> 00:04:11.633
So, you don't think
there's a connection?

00:04:12.986 --> 00:04:16.182
Connection with... First,

00:04:16.196 --> 00:04:18.512
Cattle mutilations, now...

00:04:18.518 --> 00:04:21.443
Now, two murders? Kind of
sounds like ritual stuff.

00:04:21.445 --> 00:04:24.143
You know, like satanic
cult ritual stuff.

00:04:33.287 --> 00:04:35.251
You're not kidding. No.

00:04:37.905 --> 00:04:40.470
Those cows aren't being mutilated.

00:04:40.848 --> 00:04:42.893
You want to know how I know? How?

00:04:43.205 --> 00:04:46.201
Because there's no such
thing as cattle mutilation.

00:04:46.208 --> 00:04:48.453
Cow drops, leave it in the sun,

00:04:48.457 --> 00:04:52.183
Within 48 hours the bloat
will split it open so clean

00:04:52.186 --> 00:04:53.861
It's just about surgical.

00:04:53.867 --> 00:04:57.923
The bodily fluids fall down
into the ground, get soaked up,

00:04:57.927 --> 00:05:00.230
'Cause that's what gravity does.

00:05:00.547 --> 00:05:03.431
But, hey, it could be Satan.

00:05:03.586 --> 00:05:06.553
What newspaper did
you say you worked for?

00:05:08.565 --> 00:05:10.932
World Weekly News. Weekly World News.

00:05:10.935 --> 00:05:13.772
World... I'm new. Weekly world.

00:05:15.666 --> 00:05:18.123
Get out of my office.

00:05:27.086 --> 00:05:28.043
John.

00:05:28.046 --> 00:05:30.053
Jeff. Jeff, I know that.

00:05:30.598 --> 00:05:32.873
Dr. Dorkin needs to see you
in his office right away.

00:05:32.876 --> 00:05:34.660
But dr. Dorkin's on vacation.

00:05:34.665 --> 00:05:37.230
He's back, and he's pissed,
and he's screaming for you, man.

00:05:37.235 --> 00:05:38.723
So, if i were you, I would...

00:05:44.365 --> 00:05:46.723
Hey, those satanists in Florida, they
marked their victims, didn't they?

00:05:46.737 --> 00:05:48.683
Yeah, reverse pentacle on the forehead.

00:05:49.867 --> 00:05:52.963
So much of that crap happens in Florida.

00:05:59.026 --> 00:06:00.481
All right. Open it.

00:06:01.265 --> 00:06:02.173
You open it.

00:06:03.646 --> 00:06:04.583
Wuss.

00:06:13.926 --> 00:06:15.303
Well, no pentagram.

00:06:16.068 --> 00:06:18.072
Poor girl. Maybe we should, uh,

00:06:18.077 --> 00:06:19.493
Look in her mouth, see if

00:06:19.848 --> 00:06:22.991
This wacko stuffed anything down her
throat, you know, kind of like the moth in

00:06:23.287 --> 00:06:24.551
"Silence of the Lambs".

00:06:25.195 --> 00:06:27.602
Yeah, yeah, go ahead. No, you go ahead.

00:06:28.167 --> 00:06:29.193
W hat?

00:06:29.196 --> 00:06:30.680
"Put the lotion in the basket".

00:06:31.558 --> 00:06:33.560
Right, yeah, I'm the wuss, huh?

00:06:34.436 --> 00:06:35.373
Whatever.

00:06:42.245 --> 00:06:43.563
Dean, get me a bucket.

00:06:43.585 --> 00:06:45.423
Find something? No, I'm gonna puke.

00:06:49.567 --> 00:06:51.520
All right, lift her lip up again. What?

00:06:52.818 --> 00:06:55.472
You want me to throw up, is that
it? No, I think I saw something.

00:07:00.218 --> 00:07:01.612
Is that a hole?

00:07:03.546 --> 00:07:05.763
It's a tooth. Sam, that's a fang.

00:07:08.617 --> 00:07:11.523
Retractable set of vampire
fangs. You got to be kidding me.

00:07:11.528 --> 00:07:13.400
Well, this changes things.

00:07:13.635 --> 00:07:14.673
You think?

00:07:41.835 --> 00:07:43.221
How's it going?

00:07:43.617 --> 00:07:44.720
Living  the dream.

00:07:44.725 --> 00:07:46.461
What can I get for
you? Two beers, please.

00:07:48.677 --> 00:07:50.251
So, we're looking for some people.

00:07:51.376 --> 00:07:53.050
Sure. It's hard to be lonely.

00:07:55.656 --> 00:07:56.960
Yeah, but, um,

00:07:58.505 --> 00:07:59.671
That's not what I meant.

00:08:06.806 --> 00:08:08.660
Great. So, these people

00:08:08.738 --> 00:08:10.440
Would've moved here
about six months ago,

00:08:10.445 --> 00:08:12.292
Probably pretty rowdy, like to drink.

00:08:12.298 --> 00:08:13.962
Yeah, real night owls, you know?

00:08:13.965 --> 00:08:15.880
Sleep all day, party all night.

00:08:16.007 --> 00:08:18.243
Barker farm got leased
out a couple months ago.

00:08:18.307 --> 00:08:20.501
Real winners. They've
been in here a lot.

00:08:20.597 --> 00:08:22.660
Drinkers, noisy.

00:08:23.337 --> 00:08:25.060
I had to 86 them once or twice.

00:08:28.595 --> 00:08:29.381
Thanks.

00:09:44.596 --> 00:09:46.151
Smile. What?

00:09:46.155 --> 00:09:48.522
Show us those pearly
whites. For the love of...

00:09:48.858 --> 00:09:50.710
You want to stick that
thing some place else?

00:09:50.727 --> 00:09:51.883
I'm not a vampire.

00:09:53.098 --> 00:09:53.802
Yeah, that's right.

00:09:54.025 --> 00:09:55.213
I heard you guys in there.

00:09:55.217 --> 00:09:57.181
What do you know about
vampires? How to kill them.

00:09:57.375 --> 00:09:58.561
Now, seriously, bro,

00:09:58.765 --> 00:10:00.501
That knife's making me itch.

00:10:04.506 --> 00:10:05.650
Easy there, chachi.

00:10:13.367 --> 00:10:14.113
See?

00:10:15.286 --> 00:10:16.132
Fangless.

00:10:16.458 --> 00:10:17.553
Happy?

00:10:20.585 --> 00:10:21.310
Now,

00:10:22.227 --> 00:10:23.281
Who the hell are you?

00:10:24.205 --> 00:10:26.042
Sam and Dean Winchester.

00:10:28.941 --> 00:10:29.952
I can't believe it.

00:10:30.520 --> 00:10:31.922
You know, I met your old man once.

00:10:31.920 --> 00:10:33.338
Hell of a guy, great hunter.

00:10:34.678 --> 00:10:35.703
I heard he passed.

00:10:36.225 --> 00:10:37.451
I'm sorry.

00:10:37.736 --> 00:10:38.930
It's big shoes,

00:10:39.078 --> 00:10:41.010
But, from what I hear,
you guys fill them.

00:10:41.128 --> 00:10:43.010
Great trackers, good in a tight spot.

00:10:43.058 --> 00:10:44.753
You seem to know a lot about our family.

00:10:44.757 --> 00:10:45.991
Word travels fast.

00:10:46.086 --> 00:10:48.451
You know how hunters
talk. No, we don't actully.

00:10:48.598 --> 00:10:50.600
I guess there's a lot your
dad never told you, huh?

00:10:52.976 --> 00:10:54.210
So, um...

00:10:55.906 --> 00:10:57.710
So, those two vampires,
they were yours, huh?

00:10:57.718 --> 00:10:58.641
Yep.

00:10:58.725 --> 00:10:59.681
Been here two weeks.

00:10:59.686 --> 00:11:01.622
Did you check out that
Barker farm? It's a bust.

00:11:01.626 --> 00:11:03.141
Just a bunch of hippie freaks.

00:11:03.296 --> 00:11:05.460
Though they could kill with
that patchouli smell alone.

00:11:05.465 --> 00:11:06.480
Where's the nest, then?

00:11:08.975 --> 00:11:10.121
I got this one covered.

00:11:11.206 --> 00:11:12.283
Look, don't get me wrong.

00:11:12.287 --> 00:11:13.871
It's a real pleasure meeting you fellas,

00:11:13.936 --> 00:11:15.700
But I've been on this
thing for over a year.

00:11:16.375 --> 00:11:19.370
I killed a fang back in Austin,
tracked the nest all the way up here.

00:11:19.837 --> 00:11:20.661
I'll finish it.

00:11:21.585 --> 00:11:22.893
We could help.

00:11:22.937 --> 00:11:24.073
Thanks, but, uh,

00:11:24.398 --> 00:11:26.091
I'm kind of a
go-It-Alone type of guy.

00:11:26.147 --> 00:11:27.930
But man, I've been itching for a hunt.

00:11:28.385 --> 00:11:29.163
Sorry.

00:11:29.167 --> 00:11:31.850
But, hey, I hear there's a
chupacabra two states over.

00:11:32.027 --> 00:11:33.480
Go ahead and knock yourselves out.

00:11:39.788 --> 00:11:41.381
It was real good meeting you, though.

00:11:42.427 --> 00:11:44.193
I'll buy you a drink on the flip side.

00:14:24.036 --> 00:14:25.080
So, uh,

00:14:25.398 --> 00:14:27.283
I guess I got to buy you that drink.

00:14:46.167 --> 00:14:46.942
No, no,

00:14:47.157 --> 00:14:48.002
I got it.

00:14:48.007 --> 00:14:49.411
Come on. I insist.

00:14:50.507 --> 00:14:51.401
Thank you, sweetie.

00:14:54.967 --> 00:14:56.392
Another one bites the dust.

00:14:56.397 --> 00:14:57.123
That's right.

00:15:07.465 --> 00:15:10.421
You gave that big-Ass fang one
hell of a haircut, my friend.

00:15:10.435 --> 00:15:12.002
That was you. That was beautiful,

00:15:12.016 --> 00:15:14.312
Absolutely beautiful. Yep.

00:15:15.258 --> 00:15:17.022
You all right, Sammy? Yeah, fine.

00:15:17.026 --> 00:15:18.322
Lighten up a little, Sammy.

00:15:18.535 --> 00:15:20.311
He's the only one who
gets to call me that.

00:15:20.677 --> 00:15:21.501
Okay.

00:15:21.738 --> 00:15:22.730
No offense meant.

00:15:22.736 --> 00:15:24.772
Just celebrating a
little. Job well done.

00:15:24.778 --> 00:15:26.213
Right. Well, um,

00:15:26.908 --> 00:15:30.212
Decapitations aren't my
idea of a good time, I guess.

00:15:30.216 --> 00:15:32.712
Oh,  come on, man, it's
not like it was human.

00:15:32.716 --> 00:15:34.800
You got to have a little
more fun in that job.

00:15:34.806 --> 00:15:36.670
See, that's what I've
been trying to tell him.

00:15:36.686 --> 00:15:38.480
You could learn a thing
or two from this guy.

00:15:43.006 --> 00:15:44.152
Yeah,  I bet I could.

00:15:44.506 --> 00:15:45.270
Look,

00:15:45.366 --> 00:15:46.963
I'm not gonna bring you guys down.

00:15:46.965 --> 00:15:48.493
I'm just gonna go back to the motel.

00:15:48.698 --> 00:15:49.933
You sure? Yeah.

00:15:53.305 --> 00:15:54.183
Sammy...

00:15:56.557 --> 00:15:59.082
Remind me to beat that buzzkill
out of you later, all right?

00:16:03.156 --> 00:16:04.631
Something I said? No, no.

00:16:04.635 --> 00:16:06.153
He just gets that way sometimes.

00:16:07.448 --> 00:16:08.480
Tell you what,

00:16:09.267 --> 00:16:10.920
Match quarters for the next round.

00:16:28.926 --> 00:16:29.680
So

00:16:30.155 --> 00:16:31.361
I picked up this crossbow,

00:16:31.805 --> 00:16:33.343
And I hit that ugly sucker.

00:16:33.438 --> 00:16:34.802
The silver-Tipped arrow,

00:16:35.028 --> 00:16:35.953
Right in his heart.

00:16:36.656 --> 00:16:38.413
Sammy's waiting in the car, and

00:16:38.418 --> 00:16:40.612
Me and my dad take the
thing into the woods,

00:16:41.268 --> 00:16:42.683
Burn it to a crisp.

00:16:43.097 --> 00:16:46.222
I'm sitting there, and I'm looking into
the fire, and I'm thinking to myself,

00:16:47.427 --> 00:16:48.963
I'm 16 years old

00:16:50.115 --> 00:16:52.561
Kids my age are worried about pimples,

00:16:52.565 --> 00:16:53.691
Prom dates.

00:16:54.517 --> 00:16:56.572
I'm seeing things that
they'll never even know,

00:16:57.417 --> 00:16:58.752
Never even dream of.

00:17:01.738 --> 00:17:03.192
So right then, I just sort of...

00:17:03.445 --> 00:17:04.771
Embraced the life?

00:17:06.325 --> 00:17:07.140
Yeah.

00:17:07.376 --> 00:17:08.343
Yeah.

00:17:10.085 --> 00:17:10.871
Yeah.

00:17:12.536 --> 00:17:13.672
How'd you get started?

00:17:13.678 --> 00:17:16.570
First time I saw a
vampire, I was barely 18.

00:17:16.738 --> 00:17:18.382
Home alone with my sister.

00:17:18.387 --> 00:17:21.471
I hear the window break in her room.

00:17:22.545 --> 00:17:24.450
I grabbed my dad's gun, run in,

00:17:24.457 --> 00:17:25.931
Try to get it off her.

00:17:25.936 --> 00:17:27.060
It was too late.

00:17:27.456 --> 00:17:29.000
So I shoot the damn thing,

00:17:29.306 --> 00:17:32.812
Which, of course, is about as useful
as snapping it with a rubber band.

00:17:33.065 --> 00:17:34.411
It rushes me,

00:17:34.415 --> 00:17:38.322
Picks me up, flings me across
the room, knocks me out cold.

00:17:38.327 --> 00:17:40.021
When I wake up,

00:17:40.398 --> 00:17:42.281
The vampire's gone...

00:17:42.595 --> 00:17:44.640
My sister's gone.

00:17:44.817 --> 00:17:46.151
And then?

00:17:46.285 --> 00:17:47.590
Then...

00:17:50.048 --> 00:17:51.961
Try explaining that one to your family.

00:17:53.785 --> 00:17:54.901
So I left home...

00:17:56.526 --> 00:17:59.052
And then bummed around
looking for information.

00:17:59.727 --> 00:18:01.633
How you track them, how you kill them.

00:18:03.546 --> 00:18:05.252
And I found that fang.

00:18:06.236 --> 00:18:08.023
It was my first kill.

00:18:10.005 --> 00:18:11.451
Sorry about your sister.

00:18:12.056 --> 00:18:12.892
Yeah.

00:18:14.535 --> 00:18:15.540
She was beautiful.

00:18:16.295 --> 00:18:17.962
I can still see her, you know,

00:18:18.257 --> 00:18:19.510
The way she was.

00:18:25.286 --> 00:18:27.292
But, hey, that was a long time ago.

00:18:28.088 --> 00:18:29.021
I mean,

00:18:29.028 --> 00:18:29.883
Your dad...

00:18:30.926 --> 00:18:31.961
It's got to be rough.

00:18:32.436 --> 00:18:33.332
Yeah.

00:18:35.175 --> 00:18:36.431
Yeah, you know,

00:18:36.717 --> 00:18:38.213
He was just one of those guys.

00:18:39.497 --> 00:18:40.980
Took some terrible beatings,

00:18:41.665 --> 00:18:42.920
Just kept coming.

00:18:43.917 --> 00:18:45.331
So you're always saying to yourself,

00:18:46.545 --> 00:18:47.421
He's indestructible.

00:18:48.645 --> 00:18:51.051
He'll always be around.
Nothing can kill my dad.

00:18:52.967 --> 00:18:54.071
And just like that...

00:18:56.428 --> 00:18:57.350
He's gone.

00:19:05.126 --> 00:19:07.103
I can't talk about this to Sammy.

00:19:07.576 --> 00:19:09.732
No, I got to keep my game face on.

00:19:11.076 --> 00:19:12.500
But, uh...

00:19:13.585 --> 00:19:16.301
Truth is, I'm not handling it very well.

00:19:19.486 --> 00:19:21.151
I feel like I have this...

00:19:21.157 --> 00:19:22.561
Hole inside you?

00:19:23.677 --> 00:19:26.680
And it just gets bigger and
bigger and darker and darker?

00:19:29.527 --> 00:19:30.413
Good.

00:19:31.026 --> 00:19:32.082
You can use it.

00:19:32.246 --> 00:19:33.431
Keeps you hungry.

00:19:34.267 --> 00:19:35.203
Trust me,

00:19:35.208 --> 00:19:37.780
There's plenty out there needs
killing, and this will help you do it.

00:19:39.966 --> 00:19:41.763
It's not a crime to need your job.

00:19:50.477 --> 00:19:51.531
Hardrails roadhouse.

00:19:51.587 --> 00:19:53.493
Hey, Ellen. Sam Winchester.

00:19:53.498 --> 00:19:55.682
Sam, it's good to hear from you.

00:19:56.015 --> 00:19:59.123
You boys are okay, aren't you?
Yeah, yeah, everything's fine.

00:19:59.277 --> 00:20:00.473
Got a question.

00:20:00.477 --> 00:20:01.290
Yeah, shoot.

00:20:01.297 --> 00:20:03.580
You  ever run across a
guy named Gordon Walker?

00:20:03.855 --> 00:20:05.011
I know Gordon.

00:20:05.015 --> 00:20:06.703
And? He's a real good hunter.

00:20:06.707 --> 00:20:09.383
Why you're asking, sweetie?
We ran into him on a job.

00:20:09.518 --> 00:20:12.331
We're kind of working with
him. Don't do that, Sam.

00:20:13.476 --> 00:20:14.270
I...

00:20:14.506 --> 00:20:16.241
I thought you said he was a good hunter.

00:20:16.337 --> 00:20:18.553
Yeah, and Hannibal Lecter's
a good psychiatrist.

00:20:18.568 --> 00:20:21.492
He is dangerous to everyone
and everything around him.

00:20:21.667 --> 00:20:24.470
If he's working on a job, you boys
just let him handle it and you move on.

00:20:24.547 --> 00:20:25.780
Ellen... No, Sam,

00:20:25.785 --> 00:20:27.953
You just listen to what
I'm telling you, okay?

00:20:30.176 --> 00:20:31.303
Right, okay.

00:20:31.858 --> 00:20:33.391
You know why I love this life?

00:20:34.766 --> 00:20:36.560
It's all black and white.

00:20:36.857 --> 00:20:38.100
There's no maybe.

00:20:38.426 --> 00:20:39.843
You  find the bad thing,

00:20:39.847 --> 00:20:40.571
Kill it.

00:20:41.176 --> 00:20:43.963
Most people spend their
lives in shades of gray.

00:20:44.865 --> 00:20:46.942
Is this right? Is that wrong?

00:20:47.308 --> 00:20:48.312
Not us.

00:20:48.868 --> 00:20:51.090
Not sure Sammy would
agree with you, but, uh...

00:20:51.318 --> 00:20:53.543
Doesn't seem like your
brother's much like us.

00:20:54.846 --> 00:20:56.262
I'm not saying he's wrong.

00:20:56.576 --> 00:20:57.583
Just different.

00:20:57.825 --> 00:20:58.852
You and me,

00:20:58.937 --> 00:21:00.313
We were born to do this.

00:21:00.807 --> 00:21:02.052
It's in our blood.

00:22:58.325 --> 00:22:59.200
Wait!

00:23:00.167 --> 00:23:01.562
Step back, Eli.

00:23:09.237 --> 00:23:11.450
My name's Lenore. I'm
not gonna hurt you.

00:23:11.458 --> 00:23:13.152
We just need to talk. Talk?

00:23:13.408 --> 00:23:14.383
Yeah, okay. But

00:23:14.385 --> 00:23:17.573
I might have a tough time paying
attention to much besides Eli's teeth.

00:23:17.588 --> 00:23:21.400
He won't hurt you, either. You have my
word. Your word? Oh, yeah, great, thanks.

00:23:21.405 --> 00:23:24.150
Listen, lady, no offense, but you're
not the first vampire I've met.

00:23:24.156 --> 00:23:25.672
We're not like the others.

00:23:25.687 --> 00:23:27.090
We don't kill humans,

00:23:27.097 --> 00:23:29.330
And we don't drink their blood.
We haven't for a long time.

00:23:29.378 --> 00:23:31.791
What is this? Some kinda joke?
Notice you're still alive.

00:23:36.228 --> 00:23:40.093
Okay, uh, correct me if I'm wrong here,
but shouldn't you be starving to death?

00:23:40.105 --> 00:23:41.641
We found other ways.

00:23:41.645 --> 00:23:42.541
Cattle blood.

00:23:42.916 --> 00:23:44.660
You're telling me you're
responsible for all the...

00:23:44.668 --> 00:23:47.061
It's not ideal. In
fact, it's disgusting.

00:23:47.395 --> 00:23:50.850
But it allows us to
get by. Okay. Uh, why?

00:23:50.868 --> 00:23:51.892
Survival.

00:23:52.657 --> 00:23:54.900
No deaths, no missing locals, no

00:23:54.907 --> 00:23:58.000
Reason for people like you to
come looking for people like us.

00:23:58.845 --> 00:24:00.343
And we blend in.

00:24:00.958 --> 00:24:03.053
Our kind is practically extinct.

00:24:03.335 --> 00:24:06.442
It turns out we weren't as high
up the food chain as we imagined.

00:24:06.446 --> 00:24:08.563
Why are we explaining
ourselves to this killer?

00:24:08.568 --> 00:24:10.061
Eli. We choke

00:24:10.065 --> 00:24:12.613
On cow's blood so that
none of them suffer.

00:24:12.618 --> 00:24:15.100
Tonight, they murdered
Conrad, and they celebrated.

00:24:15.107 --> 00:24:18.071
Eli, that's enough.
Yeah, Eli, that's enough.

00:24:18.077 --> 00:24:20.080
What's done is done.

00:24:20.655 --> 00:24:23.590
We're leaving this town tonight.
Then, why did you bring me here?

00:24:23.597 --> 00:24:25.430
Why are you even talking to me?

00:24:25.438 --> 00:24:27.023
Believe me, I'd rather not.

00:24:27.025 --> 00:24:28.382
But I know your kind.

00:24:28.388 --> 00:24:30.191
Once you have the scent,
you'll keep tracking us.

00:24:30.196 --> 00:24:31.601
It doesn't matter where we go.

00:24:32.168 --> 00:24:33.661
Hunters will find us.

00:24:33.806 --> 00:24:35.533
So you're asking us not to follow you.

00:24:35.537 --> 00:24:37.791
We have a right to live.
We're not hurting anyone.

00:24:37.797 --> 00:24:39.040
Right, so you keep saying.

00:24:39.096 --> 00:24:41.471
But give me one good reason
why I should believe you.

00:24:44.548 --> 00:24:45.671
Fine.

00:24:47.406 --> 00:24:49.090
You know what I'm going to do?

00:24:51.995 --> 00:24:54.250
I'm going to let you go.

00:24:57.187 --> 00:24:58.701
Take him back.

00:24:58.718 --> 00:25:00.102
Not a mark on him.

00:25:29.628 --> 00:25:32.103
This is the best
pattern I can establish.

00:25:32.397 --> 00:25:33.923
It's sketchy, at best.

00:25:33.925 --> 00:25:36.280
Looks like it's all coming
from this side of town,

00:25:36.387 --> 00:25:38.322
Which means the nest would be
around here someplace, right?

00:25:38.325 --> 00:25:39.853
Yep, that's what I'm thinking.

00:25:40.156 --> 00:25:43.562
Problem is, there's
35, 40 farms out there.

00:25:43.768 --> 00:25:45.832
I searched about half
of them already but

00:25:45.835 --> 00:25:47.131
Nothing yet.

00:25:47.275 --> 00:25:48.820
They're covering their tracks real good.

00:25:48.827 --> 00:25:50.862
I guess we'll just have
to search the other half.

00:25:53.875 --> 00:25:55.473
What time is it? Where is Sam?

00:25:56.198 --> 00:25:57.793
Car's parked outside.

00:25:58.118 --> 00:25:59.872
Probably went for a walk.

00:26:00.266 --> 00:26:03.291
Seems like the take-A-Walk
type. Yeah, he is, but...

00:26:07.328 --> 00:26:08.290
Where you been?

00:26:08.607 --> 00:26:10.112
Can I talk to you alone?

00:26:11.346 --> 00:26:12.843
You mind chilling out
for a couple of minutes?

00:26:18.985 --> 00:26:20.861
Dean, maybe we got to rethink this hunt.

00:26:20.866 --> 00:26:21.971
What are you talking about?

00:26:21.977 --> 00:26:22.960
Where were you?

00:26:24.618 --> 00:26:25.711
In the nest.

00:26:25.877 --> 00:26:26.873
You found it?

00:26:26.957 --> 00:26:28.523
They found me, man.

00:26:29.165 --> 00:26:30.892
How did you get out?
How many did you kill?

00:26:32.136 --> 00:26:33.053
None.

00:26:33.468 --> 00:26:36.462
Sam, they didn't just let you
go. That's exactly what they did.

00:26:36.548 --> 00:26:37.930
All right, well, where is it?

00:26:38.535 --> 00:26:39.982
I was blindfolded. I don't know.

00:26:40.197 --> 00:26:41.223
You got to know something.

00:26:41.226 --> 00:26:42.593
We went over that
bridge outside of town,

00:26:42.598 --> 00:26:44.571
But Dean, listen, maybe
we shouldn't go after them.

00:26:44.576 --> 00:26:46.541
Why not? I don't think
they're like other vampires.

00:26:46.628 --> 00:26:47.923
I don't think they're killing people.

00:26:47.925 --> 00:26:48.790
You're joking.

00:26:50.485 --> 00:26:51.922
Then, how do they stay alive

00:26:51.927 --> 00:26:53.583
Or undead or whatever the hell they are?

00:26:53.596 --> 00:26:54.971
The cattle mutilations.

00:26:55.048 --> 00:26:56.880
They said they live off of animal blood.

00:26:56.945 --> 00:26:58.001
And you believed them?

00:26:58.196 --> 00:26:59.191
Look at me, Dean.

00:27:00.526 --> 00:27:02.191
They let me go without a scratch.

00:27:02.746 --> 00:27:03.850
Wait, so you're saying...

00:27:05.486 --> 00:27:07.103
No, man. No way.

00:27:07.165 --> 00:27:09.211
I don't know why they let
you go. I don't really care.

00:27:09.688 --> 00:27:10.740
We find them, and we waste them.

00:27:11.486 --> 00:27:12.523
Why?

00:27:14.257 --> 00:27:16.560
What part of vampires
don't you understand, Sam?

00:27:16.567 --> 00:27:18.920
If it's supernatural, we kill
it. End of story. That's our job.

00:27:18.925 --> 00:27:21.931
No, Dean, that is not our
job. Our job is hunting evil.

00:27:22.088 --> 00:27:24.463
And if these things aren't
killing people, they're not evil.

00:27:24.477 --> 00:27:26.192
Of course, they're killing
people. That's what they do.

00:27:26.197 --> 00:27:27.650
They're all the same, Sam.

00:27:27.695 --> 00:27:29.171
They're not human, okay?

00:27:29.176 --> 00:27:30.732
We have to exterminate
every last one of them.

00:27:30.738 --> 00:27:33.541
No, Dean, I don't think so,
all right? Not this time.

00:27:33.545 --> 00:27:35.941
Gordon's been on those
vamps for a year. He knows.

00:27:35.947 --> 00:27:38.233
Gordon? You're taking his word for it?

00:27:38.237 --> 00:27:40.353
That's right. Ellen says he's bad news.

00:27:40.517 --> 00:27:41.851
You called Ellen?

00:27:42.338 --> 00:27:44.621
And I'm supposed to listen to
her? We barely know her, Sam.

00:27:44.625 --> 00:27:46.200
No thanks. I'll go with Gordon.

00:27:46.206 --> 00:27:48.693
Right, 'cause Gordon's
such an old friend.

00:27:49.665 --> 00:27:51.073
You don't think I can see what this is?

00:27:51.077 --> 00:27:52.973
What are you talking about?
He's a substitute for dad.

00:27:53.185 --> 00:27:54.933
A poor one. Shut up, Sam.

00:27:54.937 --> 00:27:57.652
He's not even close,
Dean, not on his best day.

00:27:57.658 --> 00:27:59.983
You know what, I'm not even...
You slap on this fake smile,

00:27:59.985 --> 00:28:03.052
But I can see right through it
'cause I know how you feel, Dean.

00:28:03.057 --> 00:28:04.050
Dad's dead.

00:28:04.065 --> 00:28:06.872
And he left a hole, and it
hurts so bad you can't take it.

00:28:06.878 --> 00:28:09.443
But you can't just fill up that
hole with whoever you want to.

00:28:10.185 --> 00:28:11.901
It's an insult to his memory.

00:28:14.146 --> 00:28:14.901
Okay.

00:28:26.536 --> 00:28:27.822
You can hit me all you want.

00:28:27.958 --> 00:28:28.981
It won't change anything.

00:28:29.477 --> 00:28:30.702
I'm going to that nest.

00:28:30.807 --> 00:28:32.250
You don't want to tell me where it is?

00:28:32.257 --> 00:28:33.043
Fine.

00:28:33.356 --> 00:28:34.473
I'll find it myself.

00:28:38.755 --> 00:28:39.491
Dean.

00:28:43.605 --> 00:28:44.393
Gordon?

00:28:47.296 --> 00:28:48.541
You think he went after them?

00:28:48.656 --> 00:28:49.382
Probably.

00:28:49.385 --> 00:28:51.082
Dean, we have to stop him. Really?

00:28:51.087 --> 00:28:52.700
'Cause I say we lend a hand.

00:28:52.708 --> 00:28:54.763
Just give me the benefit
of the doubt, would you?!

00:28:54.768 --> 00:28:55.880
You owe me that.

00:28:55.887 --> 00:28:56.953
Yeah, we'll see.

00:28:57.297 --> 00:28:58.603
I'll drive. Give me the keys.

00:29:02.395 --> 00:29:03.733
He snaked the keys.

00:29:04.477 --> 00:29:05.640
I can't believe this.

00:29:06.877 --> 00:29:08.443
I just fixed her up, too.

00:29:13.536 --> 00:29:15.682
So, the bridge, is that all you got?

00:29:15.726 --> 00:29:18.112
The bridge was 4 and 1/2
minutes from their farm.

00:29:18.176 --> 00:29:19.102
How do you know?

00:29:20.436 --> 00:29:21.293
I counted.

00:29:23.786 --> 00:29:27.412
Took a left out of the farm, then
turned right onto a dirt road,

00:29:27.906 --> 00:29:30.012
Followed that for two
minutes slightly uphill

00:29:30.016 --> 00:29:32.433
Then took another quick
right, and we hit the bridge.

00:29:32.745 --> 00:29:34.043
You're good.

00:29:35.166 --> 00:29:36.993
You're a monster pain in the ass...

00:29:38.225 --> 00:29:39.373
But you're good.

00:29:52.677 --> 00:29:55.283
In the truck, thank you.
We can't leave like this.

00:29:55.458 --> 00:29:56.433
Lenore,

00:29:57.238 --> 00:29:59.153
Listen to me. We need to stay and fight.

00:29:59.156 --> 00:30:01.443
They were my friends,
too, Eli, my family.

00:30:01.445 --> 00:30:03.133
That's not what I'm talking about.

00:30:03.525 --> 00:30:05.710
This is self-Defense.
Kill or be killed.

00:30:05.715 --> 00:30:07.671
They can't hunt us if they're dead.

00:30:07.858 --> 00:30:10.380
Killing those three
wouldn't solve anything.

00:30:10.886 --> 00:30:13.862
There's more where they
came from. We're outnumbered.

00:30:14.276 --> 00:30:15.370
This...

00:30:15.527 --> 00:30:17.411
This is all we can do.

00:30:17.955 --> 00:30:20.621
Try and reason... You can't
reason with these people.

00:30:21.295 --> 00:30:23.143
They're gonna kill us all anyway.

00:30:24.355 --> 00:30:26.533
We should at least take
a few of them with us.

00:30:29.988 --> 00:30:31.610
I'm not giving up hope.

00:30:33.378 --> 00:30:34.821
If we can change,

00:30:35.617 --> 00:30:36.981
They can change.

00:30:37.127 --> 00:30:40.242
Now, go into town and gather the others.

00:30:40.245 --> 00:30:42.001
We leave before sunrise.

00:32:08.966 --> 00:32:10.571
Dead man's blood, bitch.

00:32:50.385 --> 00:32:53.792
Sam, Dean, come on in.
Gordon, what's going on?

00:32:53.795 --> 00:32:56.513
Just poisoning Lenore here
with some dead man's blood.

00:32:56.515 --> 00:32:59.033
She's gonna tell us where all her
little friends are, aren't you?

00:32:59.276 --> 00:33:00.053
Want to help?

00:33:00.116 --> 00:33:01.880
Look, man... Grab a knife.

00:33:02.638 --> 00:33:04.870
I was just about to
start in on the fingers.

00:33:11.977 --> 00:33:12.913
Let's all just

00:33:13.047 --> 00:33:14.181
Chill out, huh?

00:33:14.958 --> 00:33:17.610
I'm completely chill.
Gordon, put the knife down.

00:33:17.876 --> 00:33:19.902
It sounds like it's
Sam here needs to chill.

00:33:20.068 --> 00:33:22.110
Just step away from her, all right?

00:33:27.645 --> 00:33:28.651
You're right.

00:33:30.315 --> 00:33:31.700
I'm wasting my time here.

00:33:32.525 --> 00:33:34.071
This bitch will never talk.

00:33:35.576 --> 00:33:37.612
Might as well put her out of her misery.

00:33:38.336 --> 00:33:40.842
I just sharpened it, so
it's completely humane.

00:33:41.386 --> 00:33:44.360
Gordon, I'm letting her go.
You're not doing a damn thing.

00:33:47.288 --> 00:33:49.901
Gordon, let's talk about this.
What's there to talk about?

00:33:49.906 --> 00:33:51.261
It's like I said, Dean.

00:33:51.266 --> 00:33:53.432
No shades of gray. Yeah,

00:33:53.436 --> 00:33:54.682
I hear you.

00:33:55.076 --> 00:33:57.111
And I know how you feel. Do you?

00:33:57.117 --> 00:34:00.361
The vampire that killed your
sister deserved to die, but this...

00:34:01.886 --> 00:34:03.271
Killed my sister.

00:34:04.027 --> 00:34:07.393
That filthy fang didn't kill
my sister. It turned her,

00:34:08.028 --> 00:34:09.431
Made her one of them.

00:34:09.976 --> 00:34:13.050
So I hunted her down
and I killed her myself.

00:34:14.408 --> 00:34:15.521
You did what?

00:34:15.525 --> 00:34:17.822
It wasn't my sister
anymore. It wasn't human.

00:34:18.566 --> 00:34:19.831
I didn't blink.

00:34:20.505 --> 00:34:23.293
And neither would you. So
you knew all along, then.

00:34:23.298 --> 00:34:26.010
You knew the vampires
weren't killing anyone.

00:34:26.227 --> 00:34:27.820
You knew about the cattle,

00:34:27.825 --> 00:34:30.252
And you just didn't
care. Care about what?

00:34:30.357 --> 00:34:33.013
A nest of vampires suddenly acting nice,

00:34:33.017 --> 00:34:35.691
Taking a little time out
from sucking innocent people,

00:34:35.698 --> 00:34:37.233
And we're supposed to buy that?

00:34:37.357 --> 00:34:38.272
Trust me.

00:34:39.847 --> 00:34:41.453
It doesn't change what they are.

00:34:43.285 --> 00:34:44.541
And I can prove it.

00:34:48.816 --> 00:34:49.722
Let him go.

00:34:52.527 --> 00:34:53.380
Now!

00:34:53.466 --> 00:34:56.641
Relax. If I wanted to kill
him, he'd be on the floor.

00:34:57.506 --> 00:34:58.852
Just making a little point.

00:35:14.726 --> 00:35:16.212
Think she's so different?

00:35:18.765 --> 00:35:20.673
Still want to save her? Look at her.

00:35:24.987 --> 00:35:26.212
They're all the same.

00:35:26.878 --> 00:35:27.760
Evil,

00:35:27.857 --> 00:35:29.131
Bloodthirsty.

00:35:34.865 --> 00:35:35.821
No.

00:35:36.408 --> 00:35:37.370
No.

00:35:39.645 --> 00:35:41.323
You hear her, Gordon?

00:35:41.815 --> 00:35:42.830
No.

00:35:50.086 --> 00:35:51.491
We're done here.

00:35:53.086 --> 00:35:55.073
Sam, get her out of here. Yeah.

00:36:01.886 --> 00:36:02.761
Gordon,

00:36:04.567 --> 00:36:06.723
I think you and I got
some things to talk about.

00:36:20.627 --> 00:36:21.721
Get out of my way.

00:36:22.836 --> 00:36:23.611
Sorry.

00:36:23.718 --> 00:36:24.842
You're not serious.

00:36:28.197 --> 00:36:30.721
I'm having a hard time believing
it, too, but I know what I saw.

00:36:30.727 --> 00:36:32.773
If you want those vampires,
you got to go through me.

00:36:41.167 --> 00:36:41.971
Fine.

00:37:03.105 --> 00:37:05.952
What are you doing, man?
You doing this for a fang?

00:37:06.936 --> 00:37:09.160
Come on, Dean, we're
on the same side here.

00:37:09.165 --> 00:37:11.103
I don't think so, you sadistic bastard.

00:37:16.567 --> 00:37:18.290
You're not like your brother.

00:37:18.387 --> 00:37:19.422
You're a killer

00:37:19.667 --> 00:37:20.603
Like me.

00:37:46.278 --> 00:37:47.572
Oh, sorry.

00:37:50.318 --> 00:37:51.360
You know,

00:37:52.267 --> 00:37:53.681
I might be like you.

00:37:54.737 --> 00:37:55.850
I might not.

00:38:02.077 --> 00:38:04.070
But you're the one tied up right now.

00:38:45.188 --> 00:38:46.312
I miss anything?

00:38:47.577 --> 00:38:48.362
Eh, not much.

00:38:50.175 --> 00:38:51.392
Lenore get out okay?

00:38:51.657 --> 00:38:52.353
Yeah,

00:38:52.856 --> 00:38:54.142
All of them did.

00:38:57.577 --> 00:38:59.281
Then, I guess our work here is done.

00:39:02.167 --> 00:39:03.171
How are you doing, Gordie?

00:39:04.565 --> 00:39:05.600
Got to tinkle yet?

00:39:06.465 --> 00:39:07.323
All right.

00:39:08.506 --> 00:39:09.740
Well, get comfy.

00:39:10.355 --> 00:39:13.870
We'll call someone in two or
three days, have them come out

00:39:13.878 --> 00:39:14.893
And untie you.

00:39:16.907 --> 00:39:18.240
Ready to go, Dean?

00:39:19.838 --> 00:39:20.740
Not yet.

00:39:27.318 --> 00:39:28.862
I guess this is goodbye.

00:39:30.366 --> 00:39:31.401
Well, it's...

00:39:31.858 --> 00:39:32.862
It's been real.

00:39:43.836 --> 00:39:44.850
Okay.

00:39:45.355 --> 00:39:46.361
I'm good now.

00:39:47.675 --> 00:39:48.491
We can go.

00:40:02.586 --> 00:40:04.391
Sam. Yeah?

00:40:05.446 --> 00:40:06.333
Clock me one.

00:40:07.915 --> 00:40:09.011
What? Come on.

00:40:09.125 --> 00:40:10.332
I won't even hit you back.

00:40:10.467 --> 00:40:11.280
Let's go.

00:40:13.615 --> 00:40:14.332
No.

00:40:14.986 --> 00:40:17.231
Let's go. You get a
freebie. Hit me. Come on.

00:40:17.926 --> 00:40:20.620
You look like you just went 12
rounds with a block of cement, Dean.

00:40:21.716 --> 00:40:22.813
I'll take a rain check.

00:40:26.625 --> 00:40:28.080
I wish we never took this job.

00:40:28.095 --> 00:40:29.221
It just jacked everything up.

00:40:31.157 --> 00:40:31.980
What do you mean?

00:40:35.497 --> 00:40:38.171
Think about all the hunts we
went on, Sammy, our whole lives.

00:40:38.956 --> 00:40:40.863
What if we killed things
that didn't deserve killing?

00:40:41.395 --> 00:40:43.451
You know? I mean, the way dad raised us.

00:40:43.718 --> 00:40:45.481
Dean, after what happened to mom...

00:40:47.315 --> 00:40:50.081
Dad did the best he
could. I know he did.

00:40:51.576 --> 00:40:53.023
But maybe he wasn't perfect.

00:40:53.616 --> 00:40:55.810
And the way he raised us,
to hate those things...

00:40:55.817 --> 00:40:56.940
And, man, I hate them.

00:40:57.065 --> 00:40:58.371
I do.

00:40:58.588 --> 00:41:00.851
When I killed that vampire at the
mill, I didn't even think about it.

00:41:00.868 --> 00:41:02.293
Hell, I even enjoyed it.

00:41:05.445 --> 00:41:06.781
You didn't kill Lenore.

00:41:07.417 --> 00:41:09.070
No, but every instinct told me to.

00:41:09.477 --> 00:41:11.191
I was gonna kill her. I
was gonna kill them all.

00:41:11.197 --> 00:41:12.481
Yeah, Dean, but you didn't,

00:41:12.945 --> 00:41:14.280
And that's what matters.

00:41:18.246 --> 00:41:19.452
Yeah.

00:41:23.077 --> 00:41:24.701
'Cause you're a pain in my ass.

00:41:27.838 --> 00:41:30.290
I guess I might have to stick
around to be a pain in the ass, then.

00:41:31.677 --> 00:41:32.470
Thanks.

00:41:35.558 --> 00:41:36.531
Don't mention it.



00:00:15.500 --> 00:00:17.000
